<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>
    <data noupdate="0">

        <!--
            This group is standalone by design.

            Nothing here edits a record owned by hospital_management. Manager and
            system-administrator access is granted explicitly in every ACL row,
            record rule and Python guard this module adds, rather than by mutating
            another module's implied_ids.

            group_hospital_cashier USED TO BE DECLARED HERE. It now lives in
            hospital_billing (security/hospital_billing_groups.xml), because cash
            intake is a billing act and hospital_billing (which this module
            depends on) must be able to name the group in its own ACLs and
            Python guards. Declaring it downstream made that impossible without a
            circular dependency, which is why the standalone cashier could not
            record a payment. References below now use the
            hospital_billing.group_hospital_cashier external id;
            hospital_billing's 18.0.1.5.0 pre-migration re-points the existing
            record so current members keep the group.

            Emergency authorization stays here: it is clinical governance, not
            billing.
        -->

        <record id="group_hospital_emergency_authorizer" model="res.groups">
            <field name="name">Hospital Emergency Authorizer</field>
            <field name="category_id" ref="hospital_management.module_category_hospital_management"/>
            <field name="comment">May authorize an emergency bypass, which allows clinical
                service delivery before financial clearance. Granting this group is a
                clinical-governance decision: the holder can waive every payment gate on
                an encounter. It implies no other role.</field>
        </record>

        <!--
            FRONT DESK NURSE.

            Why a group at all: the people at this hospital's entrance are nurses,
            not receptionists. Hospital Nurse already holds everything needed for
            the clinical half of that job (hospital.patient.evaluation read/write/
            create, danger-sign read, patient read/write) but is missing the intake
            half: hospital_management grants perm_create=0 to Nurse on
            hospital.patient, hospital.appointment and hospital.encounter, and only
            read on hospital.patient.card.issue. Stacking Receptionist onto a nurse
            would work, but Odoo ORs ACLs and record rules across groups, so it
            hands over the whole receptionist surface to get four create bits.

            IMPLIES Hospital Nurse, deliberately, so the clinical triage ACLs are
            inherited rather than duplicated.

            IMPLIES NOTHING ELSE. Specifically NOT:
              hospital_billing.group_hospital_cashier          (no cash intake)
              hospital_management.group_hospital_accountant    (no accounting)
              hospital_management.group_hospital_manager       (no override)
              hospital_management.group_hospital_system_administrator
              hospital_management.group_hospital_receptionist
              yoya_reception_bridge.group_hospital_emergency_authorizer

            WHAT IT ADDS on top of Hospital Nurse (security/ir.model.access.csv):
              hospital.patient              + create
              hospital.appointment          + create
              hospital.encounter            + create
              hospital.patient.card.issue   + write, + create
            and, in security/yoya_reception_rules.xml, unrestricted record rules on
            hospital.appointment / hospital.encounter / hospital.patient.card.issue,
            because the entrance triages every arrival regardless of department.
            The department-scoped Nurse rule would otherwise hide most of the queue.

            WHAT IT CANNOT DO, and where that is enforced:
              record an operational payment  hospital_billing OPERATIONAL_INTAKE_GROUPS
                                             (charge_line.py): group absent
              post accounting                assert_invoice_authorized
                                             (hospital_billing_accounting)
              start a consultation           hospital_appointment.py
                                             _assert_may_start_consultation:
                                             assigned doctor / manager / admin only
              read cash amounts              groups=OPERATIONAL_MONEY_READ on the
                                             money fields: group absent

            Assigned to NO user by this module. Membership is an operational
            decision, taken deliberately.
        -->
        <record id="group_hospital_front_desk_nurse" model="res.groups">
            <field name="name">Hospital Front Desk Nurse</field>
            <field name="category_id" ref="hospital_management.module_category_hospital_management"/>
            <field name="implied_ids" eval="[(4, ref('hospital_management.group_hospital_nurse'))]"/>
            <field name="comment">Nursing staff working the hospital entrance. Registers
                patients, opens visits and performs arrival triage. Implies Hospital Nurse
                for clinical triage rights and adds only the intake create rights Nurse
                lacks. Holds NO cash-intake, accounting, payer-authorization, emergency-
                authorization or consultation-start authority: a front desk nurse can
                triage an unpaid patient but can neither take their money nor start their
                consultation.</field>
        </record>

    </data>
</odoo>
